WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:06.230
Every single one of you, by voting conscience,
that's how you change things.

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:12.490
You change things by voting for who you believe
in.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:24.400
This is a celebration, I think it is just
the start of a really big movement,

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.120
the Libertarian movement.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:45.300
I don't feel like the fact that we voted for
Gary caused that to happen.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:50.050
It was not a vote for Trump, it was a vote
for the right thing.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.800
It was not a protest, we were voting for the
right guy.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.740
I have friends who are on both sides of the
pole.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.909
My Republican friends tell me 'Hey, a vote
for Johnson is a vote for Hillary.'

00:00:57.909 --> 00:01:01.239
My Democratic friends tell me 'Hey, a vote
for Johnson is a vote for Trump.'

00:01:01.239 --> 00:01:04.159
And what I say to them is 'A vote for Johnson
is a vote for change.

00:01:04.159 --> 00:01:07.300
It's a vote to put a third party on the map.'

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:13.100
The day after the elections is gonna be a
big hang over for America

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:17.520
and a lot of people are going to look at us Libertarians

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:23.560
and say 'You caused this. Your vote, you threw away your vote.'

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:26.140
and I'm going to say back to them 'No.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:31.580
'Cause I can look back 20 years from now and
say I voted for the Libertarian party

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:35.580
because of what I believe in and what I stood up to.'

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:39.860
The people who voted for Trump are responsible
for a Trump presidency.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:45.050
So I think that, in the primaries, that was
where that decision was made.

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:48.650
I think the Libertarians have their own voice
and they speak for themselves.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:50.290
And so I think that the results that we are
seeing tonight

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:53.440
is basically the results of a very, very flawed system.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:57.700
A very flawed debating system too, as far
as the presidential debates go.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:01.000
And so I think that these deficits have to
be accounted for somehow.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:05.660
There is a phrase that I like to hear, any
gambler likes to hear it.

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:09.020
It's called 'covering the spread.'

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:15.600
And if you look up on that map that they're
showing on TV, you'll see a lot of states

00:02:15.609 --> 00:02:17.909
where Gary Johnson covered the spread.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:31.020
And there's gonna be a lot of old party politicians
whining and crying tomorrow

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:35.080
about all the votes they should have had.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:40.540
Well you know what I say to that?

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:43.760
Your tears are delicious and your parties
will die.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:54.360
If you want our votes, if you want to win
in America,

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:59.000
then you have to deal with the issues of the racist war on drugs.

00:03:01.159 --> 00:03:05.839
You have to deal with the issue of our 20
trillion dollar national debt.

00:03:08.569 --> 00:03:14.409
You have to deal with a country that no longer
wants to send it's sons and daughters overseas

00:03:14.409 --> 00:03:17.739
to die in other countries' civil wars.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:26.220
And if you don't deal with those issues and
if you don't address Libertarian issues

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.620
then you will lose.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:32.480
Get used to it.

00:03:32.489 --> 00:03:35.860
Do you regret your vote knowing what the outcome
is now?

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:41.599
No because I don't think that us voting for
Hillary would have been any better.

00:03:41.599 --> 00:03:44.620
We voted for the candidate that deserved to
win.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:48.109
We voted for the man that should have been
our president.

00:03:48.109 --> 00:03:51.379
Two days from now, who did you vote for?

00:03:51.379 --> 00:03:54.859
Two months from now, who did you vote for?

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:05.299
Two years, twenty years, always hold your
head high, all of you, you absolutely rock,

00:04:05.299 --> 00:04:10.959
thank you very very very much for being out
here and supporting this campaign.

